// Section 17 (Shape Category Theory).
// Category theory's axioms are theorems of persistence structure.
//
// Definition 17.1 (Shape Category):
//   Objects = shapes that persist
//   Morphisms = structure-preserving maps
//   Composition = sequential application of transformation law
//   Identity morphism = trivial transformation M' = M
//
// Theorem 17.2 (Category Axioms):
//   Associativity: from determinism of f (Theorem 3.9).
//   Identity: from fixed point of minimal shape (Theorem 4.2).
//
// Theorem 17.3: Functors are structural maps between shape systems.
// Theorem 17.4: Natural transformations are coherent families.
//
// Correspondence:
//   Object = Shape, Morphism = Transformation,
//   Composition = Sequential transformation law,
//   Associativity = Determinism of f,
//   Functor = Structure-preserving map.
//
// What category theory lacks: Laws of Coherence (can't distinguish
// coherent from incoherent), emergence (postulates rather than
// derives categories), structural weight (probability at branch points).
//
// Derives from: theory.algebra.emergent-existence, theory.transformation-law
  """
}

theory/landscape.sl.content:
shape theory.landscape : theory.coherence.law0, theory.coherence.law2, theory.branching.canopy, theory.minimal {
  type: theorem
  layer: 0
