//
// Step 2 (Orthogonality): U(1) projects generators as translational
//   phases. SU(2) projects generator pairs as rotational structure.
//   Orthogonal projections: each unit is cleanly translational or
//   rotational.
//
// Step 3 (One tick = one tick): propagating at c consumes one
//   evaluation per tick. Cycling through SU(2)-complex consumes one
//   evaluation per tick. Both consume the same irreducible unit.
//
// Step 4 (Conservation): Law 2 requires preservation. One
//   evaluation of translation = one evaluation of rotation.
//   At Planck scale: E = m.
//
// Step 5 (Massive particles): carry both translational and
//   rotational structure. Massless entities carry only translational.
//   They propagate at the lattice speed limit.
//
// Inertia: a shape with all structure in angular form remains
// stationary. Moving it requires external contact to supply
// translational structure.
//
// Derives from: theory.physics.higgs, theory.physics.u1,
//               theory.coherence.law2
