//
// The Higgs defines forward chirality (left-handed in our projection).
// Law 2 (Conservation): asymmetry from nothing is forbidden.
// Canopy symmetry (Theorem 12.8): every asymmetry has a complement
// with equal structural weight.
//
// Therefore: if our universe defines left as forward, a mirror
// universe defines right as forward. This is not optional. It is
// forced by the same conservation that forces the canopy to be
// symmetric.
//
// Three chirality options, all forced:
//   Left: Law of Persistence (something must persist) -> matter
//   Right: Law 2 (balance the left) -> antimatter universe
//   Null: Law 2 (balance the pair) -> dark energy
//
// Chirality IS time direction:
//   Left-handed -> time flows "forward"
//   Right-handed -> time flows "backward" (from our perspective)
//   Null -> no net time flow (stable/constant)
//
// The mirror universe has inverted time. From their perspective,
// time flows forward normally. Our universe + mirror universe =
// time-symmetric system. Null-chirality provides stable reference.
//
// CPT symmetry is structurally guaranteed:
//   Whatever CP violation we observe, the mirror has exactly
//   opposite. Sum the projections: perfect CPT symmetry.
//   CPT is forced by the mirror structure that Law 2 requires.
//
// Derives from: theory.physics.higgs (defines forward chirality),
//               theory.coherence.law2 (no asymmetry from nothing),
